{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions","id":98875,"title":"Update me on Comics: The Thread for Comic Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T19:30:21-07:00","id":98875,"title":"Update me on Comics: The Thread for Comic Questions","content":"BEWARE SPOILER DISCUSSION POSSIBLE ON THREAD<br /> <br /> Okay I recon enough comic book geeks adjourn here that this could be a good resource for people to ask questions. I am a major comic book geek, but my erudition specializing in Marvel lost its encyclopedic edge over the last decade or so as well Ironically White Wolf sort of took primacy more often then not. So let me ask some questions that I frankly don't know where to ask, as I don't really know a good Comic forum.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Marvel</b><br /> <br /> Okay so I think Rogue recently died or something, but what is the state of her powers? I think she mastered her absorption, but what happened to her flight and strength were they permanently lost? Rogue doesn't have that whole keeps all the powers she ever had thing anymore right, I really hated that. So she had to have folks to absorb in order to do anything lately?<br /> <br /> What happened with Hercules? Does he have his powers back? Last I remember he was depowered but using a mythic panoply, did his series get canned?<br /> <br /> Whats this I keep hearing about the Hulk and Redshulk destroyed a planet by punching each other, killing Fing Fang Foom, Mindless Ones, Wendigos, and other villains. What is the deal with that, was that some sort of reality altering shenanigans or something?<br /> <br /> Whats up with Doctor Doom Lately? First of all he is like one of the craziest characters to keep track of because half the time it seems he is MIA away from Latveria. But I think he was given a couple infinity gauntlets by Reeds Daughter, and he formed a league of Dooms?<br /> <br /> What's the Deal with Carnage is he Back?<br /> <br /> What is up with Doctor Strange? Last I recall he became Sorcerer Supreme again but the Vishanti broke up and Agamatto went Crazytownbananapants. Does he still have the Eye of Agamotto or does the Title now not come with that?<br /> <br /> What is the Deal with Jubilee, is she still a draculer without mutant powers?<br /> <br /> Big question, I'm really confused on the state of Mutants. So were all the old mutants re-empowered recently or something, or are just new mutants born after the Phoenix incident? Or are people spontaneously having their X-Factor awakened? I'm really confused, the M-Day thing was kinda almost Full Retard in their explanation of how it worked. Like it stopped even mutants from having children with each other which seemed poorly defined on why. What happened with Hope Summers?<br /> <br /> Wait so Colossus still had his Juggernaut powers after he was possessed by the Phoenix, as it was recently exercised from him, was it just suppressed when he had the Phoenix or was he Phoenix Juggernaut, and therefore should have been the strongest of the Phoenix Five.<br /> <br /> The ex-phoenix five hosts have their powers in flux in different ways, so how did it effect Namor?<br /> <br /> What is the Status of Spiderman's secretly alive Daughter? Was she just vanished after he made the deal with Mephisto? Before she was secretly only know to still be alive by only a handful of people, spidey not included.<br /> <br /> <b>DC</b><br /> <br /> So is the New Fifty-Two all out? Or are they still releasing new series of the 52?<br /> <br /> How old is batman supposed to be in the present? Is he now supposed to be older then Superman? Is Superman just leagues above everyone else in power or he just tip toes above other powerhouses?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:17:59-07:00","id":100233,"title":"","content":"Colossus got Juggernauts' power, whaa?!<br /> <br /> As to the DC 52, thing, I'm a little confused myself. AFAICT, DC wants to have their cake and eat it, too, by saying that they're rebooting everything and giving us the heroes' stories from the beginning...BUT everything from the previous continuity still happened, in some form. Esp, with Batman, there doesn't seem to be any change whatsoever (maybe that was a stipulation of Grant Morrison's?), which means that he had to have spent all those years raising Robin into Nightwing (which presumably means that the Teen TItans happened), but that would also mean that he's been in action well before Superman. Is DC giving up on the notion of Supes being the first modern superhero? <br /> <br /> I also note that, as of the annual, Steel, Supergirl and Kyrpto are all back, as well. Were they reintroduced? Are we to assume that the death of Superman and the Reign of the Supermen still happened? What, exactly, was the point of rebooting the DCU, then??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T00:33:22-07:00","id":100635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions#post98875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened with Hercules?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions#post98875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does he have his powers back?</div> </div> </div> </div>The superior foes of Spider-Man are scared of him, so maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions#post98875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the deal with Jubilee? Is she still a Dracula without mutant powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the last issue of <b>Wolverine</b> I read, she is a vampire, but has sparkly powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions?p=100233#post100233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Colossus got Juggernaut's power, whaa?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Colossus has had the Gem of Cytorrak, or whatever it's called, for a few years now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions?p=100233#post100233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also note that, as of the annual, Steel, Supergirl and Krypto are all back, as well. Were they reintroduced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions?p=100233#post100233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we to assume that the Death of Superman and the Reign of the Supermen still happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They all have their own origins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions?p=100233#post100233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, exactly, was the point of rebooting the DCU, then??</div> </div> </div> </div>An attempt to recapture the &quot;glory days&quot; of the nineties in defiance of all logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T18:30:50-07:00","id":101014,"title":"","content":"<b>DC</b><br /> <br /> So what exactly was the whole Grant Morrison Situation? I know part of it was he was angry they were redoing another reboot, but I was hearing he killed off Damian Wayne to stick it to the other writers or something?<br /> <br /> Wait so the Joker flayed his face and just wears a rotting facemask out of his old face now? Infection was never an issue for the insane? And what Joker is a a brilliant hand to hand combatant just because he needs to be? It always confused me when they fluctuate in the Batman stuff. Like in the old comics and the 90s show Batman is strong and a very good Martial Artist, but he is not the strongest man in the world or leaps and bounds better then other world class martial artists. In these cases the Joker is just a slippery guy who isn't Batmans equal, he's just wiry and ruthless. Then when they go crazy and have batman be just obviously the best, and even able to take on superhumans, they then make the Joker beefed up in comparison having him snap necks left and right and go toe to toe with batman. So what the hell is the deal, Joker is just the ultimate dirty street fighter, is that it?<br /> <br /> Sometimes I feel batman would be better as its own Universe, that way they wouldn't dilute things just to explain Batman outshining Super and Galactic beings. Its cool seeing batman take on robots, or the occasional car tossing foe. But something is lost when you keep switching from gotham level foes to Darkseid and Brainiac. I mean how do I take his troubles with Penguin and Joker seriously compared to Darkseid. I see him Kung Fu Solomon Grundy, but then exert the same effort with Bane. Clearly Solomon Grundy and Bane are on two different leagues of Super Strength.<br /> <br /> I love Batman, but I hate them Mary Sue him just to prove Batman is the best always.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:39:41-07:00","id":101983,"title":"","content":"<br /> I don't know what was going on with Morrison behind the scenes, I just know that I personally find his latest run at DC to have been disastrous. Final Crisis was utterly botched and nigh unintelligible, and I couldn't stand what he did with Batman...and I say this as someone who is genereally a fan of his work. So, of course, when DC rebooted everything, the one thing they made sure to keep intact was everything he had done (groan). I speculate that he may have forced them to by promising not to work there again if they didn't, and that they agreed since he's a big name with a legion of fans, but I don't really know. I just know that Dan DiDio, head of DC, outright admitting to not understanding ANY of Morrison's FC scripts, but simply rubberstamping them as he just assumed that they must be brilliant...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As to the Joker, the only time I recall his combat ability being mentioned was when the Cassandra Cain Batgirl broke him out of arkham to kick his ass (long story), and found that her ability to read body language actually made her MORE vunerable to him, as she couldn't predict his crazed, impulsive movements. She lucked out and brought him down, but just barely, and that's saying something. And they do say that &quot;the mad have strength&quot;...<br /> <br /> The &quot;Bat God&quot; phenomena you describe has bugged fans for years. If you'll note, he usually slips into that mode when with the JLA, as the writers feel the need to compensate for his lack of superpowers there more. In his own books, or with the Gotham Knights, he's much more subdued. Once you notice that pattern, it may bother you less, as it does me. YMMV...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:00:29-07:00","id":102002,"title":"","content":"Yeah that seems about right. I wish DC never had that whole, power=equals better hero schtick. Batman is cool and doesn't need to be mary sued. And while most of Superman's career has been as the Alpha of DC, his original design as just a strong, tough, quick man was excellent in that it had limits. It would have been cool to have a DC universe where he was at that powerlevel, then he could grow as a character to show him say overcoming stronger foes. I mean he was already a very potent super hero being faster then sound, and stronger then a train. There is a tough balance with Superheroes. They don't seem to like to keep heroes at a level where they are say stronger then Spiderman without boosting it waaaay out there. Its like okay either you can throw a truck or you can't. But if we have you throwing a truck we won't stop there, you will throw a train or a sentinel too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:45:25-07:00","id":102028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions?p=101983#post101983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, of course, when DC rebooted everything, the one thing they made sure to keep intact was everything he had done (groan).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true. They also kept a lot of the Blackest Day crap Johns had done with the Green Lantern franchise, which made the Green Lantern books basically impenetrable to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:59:15-07:00","id":102036,"title":"","content":"Yeah basically when people explained the new 52 to me they said everything got rebooted but Batman and Green Lantern are essentially the same somehow... even though history must be different.<br /> <br /> What is the significance of 52? Someone told me it was 52 universe of DC, or was it 52 new comics under the reboot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T18:52:53-07:00","id":102296,"title":"","content":"Fifty-two weeks in a year and fifty-two titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:30:51-07:00","id":102761,"title":"","content":"After reading this, it makes me so glad I gave up on the X-Men. Jubilee a vampire? Colossus with Juggernauts powers? Rogue dead or having some weirdness with her powers. I hear they're gonna kill Wolverine off(again again) for reals this time...for now. wink.<br /> <br /> I miss the X-Men. I used to be a huge fan...now, just not into it. I'm not a fan of the direction Marvel started taking things, so I moved on. Sad...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 03-31-2014, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T11:41:18-07:00","id":102812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/98875-update-me-on-comics-the-thread-for-comic-questions?p=102761#post102761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading this, it makes me so glad I gave up on the X-Men. Jubilee a vampire? Colossus with Juggernauts powers? Rogue dead or having some weirdness with her powers. I hear they're gonna kill Wolverine off(again again) for reals this time...for now. wink.<br /> <br /> I miss the X-Men. I used to be a huge fan...now, just not into it. I'm not a fan of the direction Marvel started taking things, so I moved on. Sad...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the eternal problem though. Characters become static. It's not terribly interesting or selling to have characters do exactly the same iconic things they've done for the last 40 years. It doesn't sell comics. So you need to change things up, kill them off, give them other problems out of left field, make the more powerful or dramatically weaker. Unfortunately after a while, that just gets into pushing them so far away from what they were, they're no longer recognizable as the same characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:34:33-07:00","id":102854,"title":"","content":"Yea, that's the double edged sword of it. And I totally get it. Just makes me miss it. Of course, I have my old comics and I can re-read them anytime I want. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T17:02:44-07:00","id":103005,"title":"","content":"It is wonky, with everything going on. But the Uncanny Avengers has been the bestest big deal title that they have going on right now! Apocalypse's Heirs, Celestials, Thor, Mutants whining you have it all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:51:22-07:00","id":103463,"title":"","content":"The old 60s stuff was awesome. and when they hit their peak 20 years later, it was even more so.<br /> Certain select titles that I think might have been worth keeping up, but the 90s saw too much crap going on.<br /> <br /> I am of the opinion that the &quot;Thunderbolts&quot; was one title that I found out belatedly worth keeping tabs on. (At this point in time trying to catch up on that one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind w